vitrail
=======

A coupled CBCT-IOS encoder that carries one set of weights across four dental
tasks. A volumetric stream reads the cone-beam volume, a surface stream reads the
intraoral mesh as per-tooth regional tokens, and a lead-came cross-attention block
joins the two without a registration step. Four lightweight lights hang off the
shared field: 42-class CBCT segmentation, per-vertex IOS tooth labelling,
CBCT-IOS fusion / tooth-bone reconstruction, and implant-fixture detection.

The pretraining objective pulls FDI-matched teeth together across the two
modalities (InfoNCE), reconstructs masked volume blocks, and holds the volumetric
field steady when the surface stream is dropped.


bench layout
------------

  src/vitrail/atelier    seeds, logging, pydantic config schema, checkpoint panes
  src/vitrail/cutline    volume patches, surface tokenisation, the planted cohort
  src/vitrail/cartoon    volumetric encoder, surface encoder, projection, coupling
  src/vitrail/leading    the cross-attention came (Eq. 2)
  src/vitrail/soldering  InfoNCE / masked recon / consistency / segmentation losses
  src/vitrail/lights     the four task heads and the multi-task window
  src/vitrail/lightbox   Dice / mIoU / HD95 / ASSD / Chamfer, ECE, DeLong, Holm
  src/vitrail/bench      Algorithm 1 pretraining, Algorithm 2 fine-tuning, EMA, DDP
  src/vitrail/studio     command line: pretrain, finetune, appraise, etch

Configuration is layered pydantic. A panel file under configs/panels is one full
TopConfig; component fragments under configs/encoder, configs/regimen and
configs/cohorts document the pieces. Runtime knobs (device, worker count, output
directory) come from VITRAIL_* environment variables or the --device / --out-dir
flags.


raising the bench
-----------------

  python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
  python -m pip install --no-deps -e .

conda:

  conda env create -f environment.yml
  conda activate vitrail

container:

  docker build -t vitrail .
  docker run --gpus all vitrail pretrain --config configs/panels/main.yaml


glass
-----

Collections, roles and licenses live in glass-sources.txt; benchwork/gather_glass.sh
prints the resolution list. Three evaluation cohorts (Teeth3DS+, Tunisia, IOS;
ToothFairy2, Italy, CBCT; paired CBCT-IOS, China, fusion) plus the MMDental and
CTooth auxiliary CBCT corpora. The landmark co-registration that ships with the
paired collection is used only as the distance reference frame at scoring time and
never reaches the model. Volume voxels are resampled to 0.30 mm and read as 128^3
patches; surfaces are grouped into 32 FDI region slots of 256 points each.


pretraining
-----------

  bash benchwork/raise_panel.sh                       # 8-GPU torchrun, main panel
  python -m vitrail.studio pretrain --config configs/panels/main.yaml --device cuda

Writes runs/main_encoder.pane (atomic; the pane stores the seed and is restored on
resume).


fine-tuning and reading the lights
----------------------------------

  python -m vitrail.studio finetune --config configs/panels/main.yaml \
      --task seg_cbct --pretrained runs/main_encoder.pane --device cuda

  python -m vitrail.studio appraise --config configs/panels/main.yaml \
      --task seg_cbct --pane runs/main_seg_cbct.pane --device cuda

Task ids: seg_cbct, seg_ios, fusion, implant. Targets from the manuscript, scored on
the held-out split of each cohort:

  seg_cbct   ToothFairy2 mean Dice 0.9312 +/- 0.004, tooth Dice 0.943, HD95 14.8 mm
  seg_ios    Teeth3DS+ Dice 98.74 +/- 0.22, mIoU 78.9 +/- 0.4
  fusion     paired-China ASSD 0.122 +/- 0.010 mm, Chamfer-L1 0.076 +/- 0.005
  implant    ToothFairy2 implant-class proxy Dice 53.1 +/- 1.4; external Dice 44.6 +/- 2.4

Ablations are separate panels: ablation_no_crossmodal, ablation_no_fusion,
ablation_no_modality_dropout.


etching the encoder
-------------------

  python -m vitrail.studio etch --config configs/panels/main.yaml \
      --pane runs/main_encoder.pane --out runs/encoder.onnx

Exports the volumetric stream (volume -> dense field) at opset 17 with a dynamic
batch axis.


compute budget
--------------

The reported numbers come from 8x A100-80GB in fp32 with no automatic mixed
precision. Effective batch is micro_batch 2 x grad_accum 64 x world_size 8 = 1024.
Pretraining runs 4000 epochs at lr 2e-7 (200-epoch warmup, cosine decay); each task
head fine-tunes for up to 600 epochs at head lr 1e-5 with the encoder trailing at
2e-7. fp32 128^3 convolutions are the memory ceiling, not the parameter count
(62.4M). Expect this to occupy the full node for days, not hours. The dependency set
is pinned to torch 2.0.1 + cu118 on python 3.9; newer stacks change the 3D
convolution kernels and shift the third decimal of every metric above.

The _smoke panel (configs/panels/_smoke.yaml) exists only for the test bench; it is
not a reduced-cost training recipe and must not be used for any reported figure.


checkpoints
-----------

Released panes carry their training seed and tag. A pretrained encoder pane and the
four fine-tuned task panes are available upon reasonable request; each is published
with a SHA-256 manifest.
